   "id": 507830,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Solve <span data-math=\"3x-7-\\left( {x + 5} \\right) = 2\\left( {x-6} \\right).\">3x-7-\\left( {x + 5} \\right) = 2\\left( {x-6} \\right).</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"3x - 7 - \\left( {x + 5} \\right) = 2\\left( {x - 6} \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Simplify each side as much as possible.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3x - 7 - x - 5 = 2x - 12\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x - 12 = 2x - 12\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Collect the variable terms on one side.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x - 12 - 2x = 2x - 12 - 2x\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\" - 12 =  - 12\"></span></p>\n<p>This statement is always true. The variable does not matter at all, so there are infinitely many solutions.</p>\n"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\" - 12 =  - 12\"> - 12 =  - 12</span>, which is true; therefore, this is a true statement, and there are infinitely many solutions."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
